<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<sdf version="1.9">
  <!-- Physics-only ground. NO visual: this model exists solely to provide
       the corridor worlds' ground contact, decoupled from whatever is
       rendered above it.

       Why this exists (2026-07-23): a <plane> collision shape is an INFINITE
       half-space - <size> bounds only a visual, never the collision extent.
       The corridor worlds previously tiled model://textured_ground 8x to build
       a 160 m checkerboard, which stacked 8 exactly-coincident infinite
       collision planes at z=0. Contact solving over coincident surfaces is
       degenerate and cost grows superlinearly: measured RTF 0.3965 (1 plane)
       -> 0.0432 (5 planes) -> 0.0134 (8 planes), with gz sim pegging one core.
       That was the true root cause of Known Issue #11, previously misattributed
       to machine speed.

       All three corridor worlds include THIS model, identically, exactly once,
       and their floor tiles are visual-only. That guarantees the physics below
       the visual layer is bit-identical across textured / blank / transition,
       so floor texture really is the only variable - which the previous design
       did not achieve (it had 8 vs 5 vs 1 collision planes).

       <size> is present for schema completeness only and is ignored for
       collision; the half-space spans the whole world regardless. -->
  <model name="ground_collision">
    <static>true</static>
    <link name="link">
      <collision name="collision">
        <geometry>
          <plane>
            <normal>0 0 1</normal>
            <size>20 170</size>
          </plane>
        </geometry>
      </collision>
    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
